"""skhealth: lightweight infrastructure health checks with deduplicated alerts.

One short-lived process per systemd timer tick (no daemon, no container).
Python standard library only. Every external command is called by the
absolute path in the config's "bin" map: schedulers run with a minimal PATH.

Commands:
  skhealth [run]     run the checks, alert on state changes, save the state
  skhealth check     run the checks and print the problems (no alert, no state)
  skhealth --test    send one test message through every configured channel
  skhealth status    print the saved state (no secrets)

Options: --config PATH (default /etc/skhealth/skhealth.json).
"""
